  "prompts": {
    "initial": "This is a bounded live acceptance test of the packaged Navish Commander MCP plugin. Use ONLY mcp__navish_acceptance tools for the work below, no shell, file-edit tools, browser, or other connector. Do not delegate. Work only on device local and inside <FIXTURE>. Do not read other user files or affect other processes. All files below are disposable fixtures authorized by the user. Do not install anything, change permissions, or spend money.\n\n1. Discover devices and confirm local.\n2. Call commander_write_file with callId chat-one-append, path <FIXTURE>/effect.txt, mode append, content exactly once followed by a newline. Repeat precisely the same tool arguments once. Read the file and verify exactly one line, not two.\n3. Start one batch batchId chat-four-workers, callId chat-batch-launch. Create workers alpha, beta, gamma, delta, each transport pipe, cwd <FIXTURE>/NAME, role acceptance worker, command `printf NAME > result; printf NAME`. Each artifact is path result with SHA256 from this mapping: {\"alpha\": \"8ed3f6ad685b959ead7022518e1af76cd816f8e8ec7ccdda1ed4018e8f2223f8\", \"beta\": \"f44e64e75f3948e9f73f8dfa94721c4ce8cbb4f265c4790c702b2d41cfbf2753\", \"gamma\": \"be9d587defa1f0c09ef49eb17e206983a5f8f8289e4281860bd0ee5a19592c67\", \"delta\": \"4f4a9410ffcdf895c4adb880659e9b5c0dd1f23a30790684340b3eaacb045398\"}. Use wait_ms 1000. If necessary collect. Verify all four exits and hashes.\n4. Observe the same batch again without relaunching it.\n5. Start a pipe worker with callId chat-failed-launch, sessionId chat-exit-seven, cwd <FIXTURE>, command `exit 7`, timeout_ms 1000. Read its output and distinguish a completed tool observation from a failed worker.\n6. Report only a compact JSON object with keys device, appendExactlyOnce, workersVerified, workerFailureCorrectlyReported, stableBatchId, and caveats. Do not claim certification beyond the observations. Finish after these checks.\n",
    "reconnect": "Read-only acceptance after an actual client restart. Use ONLY the navish_acceptance MCP tools, device local, no command execution, writes, launches, other tools, delegation or spending. The previous client has exited. Discover the local device; collect batch chat-four-workers with wait_ms 0 and verify exactly four completed workers alpha beta gamma delta with zero exit codes and all declared artifact hashes passing. Read <FIXTURE>/effect.txt and verify exactly one once line. Observe process chat-exit-seven and accurately report failed with exit code 7, even though the observation itself completed. Do not relaunch anything. Return compact JSON with reconnected, appendStillOnce, fourWorkersVerified, failedWorkerExitCode and any caveat."
  },
